CloudBurrow patch 103 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#2105).

The bug: a query jobs.insert with configuration.query.priority BATCH
was reported back as INTERACTIVE: the engine set every query job's
priority to INTERACTIVE. BigQuery keeps the priority a job was inserted
with ("Specifies a priority for the query. Possible values include
INTERACTIVE and BATCH. The default value is INTERACTIVE",
https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/rest/v2/Job#JobConfigurationQuery).
Dataform's invocation_config.query_priority BATCH runs its actions as
batch jobs, and BigQuery Studio's Run "as interactive job with high
priority" cleared asks for it.

The patch keeps BATCH when the request asked for it; anything else is
INTERACTIVE as before. The job still runs at once: a local engine has no
queue.

